description: Coding style, refactoring, and quality standards
alwaysApply: true
---

## General Code Quality Rules

- Prefer clarity over cleverness
- Small methods
- Single responsibility
- Explicit naming
- Avoid magic numbers, use contants

---

## DRY (But Not Prematurely)

- Duplicate code is acceptable until intent is clear
- Refactor ONLY when duplication represents the same concept

---

## Refactoring Rules

- Refactors must not change behavior
- Specs must remain green
- Prefer extracting objects over conditionals

---

## Naming

- Names must reflect business intent
- Avoid technical names in domain code
- Prefer:
  - `SearchRun`
  - `CandidateSelector`
  - `AnalysisSnapshot`

---

## Method Length

- Aim for ≤ 10 lines
- If longer, extract

---

## Conditionals

- Prefer guard clauses
- Avoid nested conditionals

---

## Comments

- Explain WHY, not WHAT
- Code should explain WHAT

---

## When in Doubt

- Ask before implementing
- Do not invent behavior
- Follow domain specs strictly
